      "at": "2026-08-13T09:33:00Z",
      "scope": "change",
      "made_by": "user",
      "decision": "Approved omitting a CSRF token on POST /ui/lang/switch, CONDITIONAL on the lang cookie being SameSite=Lax",
      "why": "The module has a close CSRF precedent (vehicle-select, handlers.go:529) but it is auth-only and cannot transplant to a control that must work for anonymous login-page visitors without minting a session for every one of them. SameSite=Lax blocks the cross-site POST; worst-case abuse is a one-click-reversible language flip.",
      "covered_by": null
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "at": "2026-08-13T09:33:00Z",
      "scope": "change",
      "made_by": "leader",
      "decision": "Amended design.md D8 and tasks T2.1/T3.5 to make SameSite=Lax explicit and test-enforced",
      "why": "The worker's design never mentioned SameSite, and T2.1 specified gin's c.SetCookie(...) which has NO SameSite parameter \u2014 as written it would have produced a cookie without the attribute, silently voiding the premise the user approved. Added the mandatory c.SetSameSite call, the full normative cookie-attribute spec, and a non-droppable TestLangSwitch_CookieIsSameSiteLax.",
      "covered_by": "change Decision D1"
    },
    {
